From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:59:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: stop a burst once its station dozes

With hardware PS buffering, mt76_txq_send_burst() gives a dozing
station one frame per AC at a time and holds the rest in mac80211's
txqs. It checks MT_WCID_FLAG_PS only before the burst's first frame,
though: when the PS sync event that sets it arrives while a burst is
going out (mt7915 handles them in its MCU NAPI, maybe on another CPU),
the burst carries on and hands the dozing station's frames to the
hardware until the ring, AQL or the txq stops it. Those are the frames
the PS buffering keeps from the firmware, which loses some of what it
holds for a dozing station with the 2026-05 firmware (mt76 #1163).

Check the flag for each frame of the burst, and leave the rest to the
PS path: the txq goes back on the active list, and the next round
finds the station dozing and its airtime pending.

The power save simulation that follows (tests/ps-sim-test.c, its
mid-burst case) found it:
1397 frames in a run went to the hardware past the one per AC while
held; none with this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index 2bae1b3b..81f8df12 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -590,6 +590,14 @@ mt76_txq_send_burst(struct mt76_phy *phy, struct mt76_queue *q,
 		if (stop || mt76_txq_stopped(q))
 			break;
 
+		/*
+		 * The station began to doze while the burst went out (its PS
+		 * sync event, on another CPU): the rest waits, as for any
+		 * dozing station, instead of piling up in the hardware.
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &wcid->flags))
+			break;
+
 		skb = mt76_txq_dequeue(phy, mtxq);
 		if (!skb)
 			break;
